# Docker build-context exclusions for book-renderer (memory-book-5c plan,
# Step 3 — this directory is pulled into the render worker's image build as
# a NAMED build context: `docker build --build-context bookrenderer=../book-renderer …`
# from render/memory-book-renderer/, so THIS file is what Docker/BuildKit
# actually enforces for that context — see render/memory-book-renderer/
# Dockerfile's own header comment and README's "PII safety" section).
#
# book-data/ is the load-bearing line: 1.9GB of real exported family books
# (child PII) used for local dev/CLI iteration. It must never reach the
# render worker's image. vite.print.config.ts (publicDir: false, print.html
# entry only) is the OTHER half of this guarantee — this file is the one
# that keeps the raw directory out of the build context in the first place,
# so a build-time bug in that config can't accidentally copy it anyway.
book-data/
book-data

# Build outputs (rebuilt fresh at image-build time — never trust a stale
# host-machine dist/).
dist/
dist-web/
dist-print/

node_modules/
.git/
.env*
*.log
coverage/
